<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh six-mth T-bill av yield falls to 16.24 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh six-mth T-bill av yield falls to 16.24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of six-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 16.24 percent at an auction on Monday from 19.90 percent at the last auction on May 12, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>The authorities increased the issue volume because of heavy demand.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					 May 26	    May 12</p>
<p> Series number		     KZ46K2711971    KZ46K1311971</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)     750		  700</p>
<p> Bids (nominal)		     2,830		3,030</p>
<p> Sold (nominal)			 792		  700</p>
<p> Average price			92.49 pct	  90.95</p>
<p> Average yield			16.24 pct	  19.90</p>
<p> Tenor				  182 days	   182 days</p>
<p> Maturity			     Nov 27, 1997     Nov 13, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
